{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets","id":196703,"title":"Lambda Gadgets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-14T05:51:03-07:00","id":196703,"title":"Lambda Gadgets","content":"I have to say I'm shocked that no one has already started a thread about this, <br /> <br /> So what combinations of embeds or exploits have you folks come up with?<br /> <br /> Like one of the first things I thought of was combining Ephemeral Cover with Terrible Avatar so that their independent form takes on spirit or ghostly form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T06:22:11-07:00","id":196728,"title":"","content":"There's absolutely heaps you could do with it. A few combinations I like:<br /> <br /> Ellipses + The Map Is Not The Territory: Not only distracts someone, but also makes them useless at being able to understand any written or printed material. It'd work great for anyone front of house who deals with accounting, books or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Miles Away + Just Bruised: Gives you mental and emotional strength!<br /> <br /> Identity Theft + Going Native or The Voting Dead + Going Native: Become a flawless replica of a human for a short period of time.<br /> <br /> The Look + Knockout Punch: Put someone to sleep with your death glare <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Vox + Solitary Confinement: Contain someone to a dimension where only you can talk to them. As any voice you wish. Hell of an interrogation chamber.<br /> <br /> Authorised + The Word: Issue commands from a position of authority.<br /> <br /> Open-And-Shut-Case + Play Possum: Make it look like someone's murdered you, but come back to life later. Good for faking your own death <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cause And Effect + Murder By Improbability: Yes, you now can actually murder the prime minister by making breakfast.<br /> <br /> In My Pocket + Rip The Gates: ...on second thought, Rip The Gates as a gadget alone is terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T07:31:18-07:00","id":196779,"title":"","content":"...some of those violate the concept.<br /> <br /> Lambda Gadgets are both more versatile and more limited than the Embeds and/or Exploits they are made from. And personally, I find those restrictions to be equally as fun the powers.<br /> <br /> So please, don't let it be X + Y = Kweel.<br /> <br /> For example, instead of <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=196728#post196728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cause And Effect + Murder By Improbability: Yes, you now can actually murder the prime minister by making breakfast.</div> </div> </div> </div>imagine a black twisted piece of metal that was at point a spoon. When you use it stir some kind of food and/or drink; holding the 'spoon end' and whisper the words &quot;Eternal Sleep&quot; in perfect Cantonese (while spending a point of Ather); you may name one person. If this individual consumes the prepared food/drink within a time limit; then said meal will conspire to end that person's life.<br /> <br /> To me, that is more iconic and cool. And now I want my Killer Spoon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T14:24:12-07:00","id":198235,"title":"","content":"A second-order Lambda:<br /> <br /> Deep Cover + Visions of Heaven and Hell + Voice of the Machine: Leverage the energy released by a Falling angel to turn a demon into an exile or a stigmatic into a Fractal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T22:51:51-07:00","id":198569,"title":"","content":"The Traffic Bumper:<br /> <br /> <i>You've spent a half hour closing in on the suspect's black Lamborghini LP570-4. Damn fine car, really, but your contact has assured you that the driver is planning a terrorist action again the Deva Corporation, so you close in, hoping to... what a minute... did they? They didn't.<br /> <br /> They did.<br /> <br /> Someone actually marred that beautiful car with a bumper sticker. As you pull in behind them you see what it says &quot;How's my Driving? Call 1-800-BIG-BRO&quot;<br /> Your mind sparks, what they hell? What they hell? You don't draw attention to a car like that! Are these people trying to be subtle? <b>Funny</b>? It's bad enough they're driving around in a Red Mercedes Benz SL R230... wait.. that's what they were driving, right? Wait a minute, did you just think 'were'? With a start, you realize that the target car is nowhere to be seen,</i> and you can't remember what it looks like.<br /> <br /> Ellipsis + Never Here<br /> <br /> This magnetic bumper sticker might say anything: something political, something thoughtful, something funny but most often something inane... but it is eye catching, especially to anyone trying to shadow the car the Traffic Bumper is attached to. To activate the gadget, the car driver rolls Manipulation + Drive - Shadower's resolve. Success means the shadower stops paying attention to the target car <i>juuuussst</i> as it makes a turn until it passes out of sight. Each additional success causes the pursuer to forget one detail about the car (color, make, model, license plate number, etc.) <br /> <br /> The Sixth Bullet:<br /> <br /> <i>It's a magnum .44 round, shiny silver casing. If you hold it up to your ear, you can hear, faintly, the sound track from </i>Dirty Harry<i> coming from it.</i><br /> <br /> Like the Movies + Combustion<br /> <br /> Any car by this bullet will explode. Dramatically. The gadget can be reused by reloading the spent cartridge with propellant and a cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T16:38:30-07:00","id":203298,"title":"","content":"Armistice of Mind Home Security System<br /> <br /> <i>It looks like one of the security alarms you buy at Home Depot, if the security system was a hypothetical love child of H. R. Geiger and Rube Goldberg. 70s technological aesthetic on the front with copper screen microphones, knobs and raised grey numerical pads. Terrifying mechanical insect-like with barbered hooks scuttle on the back and, oh god, is that battery on the back leaking glowing blue ooze? </i><br /> <br /> Terrifying Avatar + Demon House<br /> <br /> Some Inquisitor, more paranoid than most, took a self install home security system, imprinted it with a copy of his personality and turned it into this. This gadget has one single purpose: if an individual enters the premises without entering the proper security code, the alarm system will possess the house, and violently try to murder the intruder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 07-11-2016, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T00:44:32-07:00","id":203597,"title":"","content":"Another second-order:<br /> <br /> High of Birth + Strength Through Adversity + Fractal Reality:<br /> <img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/eschatontology.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:22:07-08:00","id":746772,"title":"","content":"Rip The Gates+Newton's Nightmares+Echoing Death=???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T13:58:13-08:00","id":747423,"title":"","content":"Raze Infrastructure + Behind the Curtain = They Set Us Up The Bomb. By means of planting this device inside a piece of Infrastructure, it begins burning down every single one in the area (including its host Infrastructure. Something a Demon might use when they tire of existence and want to get the Machine's attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T15:17:04-08:00","id":747574,"title":"","content":"Merciless Gunman + Rip The Gates = a gun that sends the target into one of the Invisible Realms instead of dealing damage.<br /> <br /> Turn Blade + Cause And Effect = a bracelet or wristwatch that redirects the kinetic energy of a melee attack to the attacker, hurting him instead of you. A different version does the same to bullets. Does not work if the user is surprised, unless Strike First/Check Backdrop is added to the Gadget.<br /> <br /> Hellhound + Solitary Confinement = a pok\u00e9ball containing a Cryptid.<br /> <br /> Never Here + Homogeneous Memory + The Only Word That Matters = a MIB style device that causes amnesia about something the target just saw, and replaces the memory with one of the user's choosing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-23-2015, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:14:43-08:00","id":747690,"title":"","content":"<b>Across the Room + Force Relationship</b> = A flip phone where the numbers on the keypad are in Glagolitic and the symbol \u2c03 is etched deeply into screen. The shell is pretty heavily nicked, to the point where you can only vaguely tell that it was one enamelled a bright cherry red.<br /> <br /> There's no contact list and no sim card - attempting to dial a phone number just brings up static. Instead, dialling <i>any</i> unique numerical designation a person might have lets them receive the call - their cell-phone rings, the nearest fax machine prints the message in real time, their computer opens a voice-only Skype call, or the intercom system in the prison they are being kept in starts bellowing out the message in question.<br /> <br /> If anyone else tries to intercept the message or answers the phone, they hear the target's name before the connection seemingly melts into static.<br /> <br /> <b>Common Misperception + Urban Legend + Everybody Knows</b> = This Lambda was an... accident. We think. Basically, it &quot;uploads&quot; a very specific use of Common Misperception into a normal mortal person, and makes it contagious - the victim rolls their Science + Manipulation while sharing that &quot;fact&quot;, causing that use of Common Misperception (with that number of Successes) to lodge itself in the person their talking to, penalizing the next relevant roll <i>and</i> turning them into a vector of the Lambda.<br /> <br /> A given person remains a vector indefinitely - fortunately, the Lambda &quot;breaks&quot; on exposure to facts counter to the information it contains, removing itself from the person.<br /> <br /> As for <i>what</i> that fact is, well... we're not exactly <i>sure</i>. We think we might be vectors, so we don't want to guess, in case we might infect other people. You understand, right?<br /> <br /> <b>Show of Power + Inflict Stigmata + Deep Cover + Going Native</b> = While this Device appears to be a large RFID chip, looking at it under a microscope reveals that the soldering is chemically identical to human bone, while the whole chip is built on a piece of ceramic seemingly shaved from a piece of crockery. More importantly, surgically inserting this Lambda under the skin of a mundane mortal converts them into an Offspring, with some rather... interesting differences.<br /> <br /> Namely, they do not read as an Offspring or, indeed, as related to the God-Machine at all. Instead, they appear to be an <i>entirely</i> different sort of phenomena, with their Stigmata, Embeds, and Cipher twisting to match. Worryingly enough, this modification to the basic template lacks the &quot;usual&quot; Omen Sensitivity and Unseen Sense - instead, the artificial Offspring gains Unseen Sense (Others Like Me) and may convert other mortals into Stigmatics warped to follow the thematics of their &quot;type&quot; of Supernatural being by forcing them to suffer a unique Breaking Point defined by their &quot;template&quot;.<br /> <br /> Such Stigmatics also lack Omen Sensitivity and replace Unseen Sense (God-Machine) with Unseen Sense (Others Like Me) - however, rather than being contagious, they receive one of the original Offspring's Cipher Embeds instead, which must be one that the Offspring has already &quot;unlocked&quot;. Such Stigmatics receive the Swooning Condition with regards to the Offspring that &quot;turned&quot; them.<br /> <br /> It is assumed that at one point a way to reprogram the chip existed - however, after the creator (a Tempter) seems to have disappeared, and they didn't write <i>any</i> of that crap down, so the results seem to be random. We also aren't entirely sure what they were aiming to achieve - it's a cute trick, but I (at the very least) don't really see the point.<br /> <br /> <b>Wave Function Collapse + Frozen In Time + Newton's Nightmare</b> = It looks like someone had the idea to make a watch into a piece of modern art. Also, it does nothing. No really, it does <i>nothing</i> except wind down. It's stuck with regards to the frame of reference it's in when you wind it - you stick it in a train, and it moves with the train, but otherwise? Any attempt to move it or make it <i>do</i> something fails. It modifies the laws of physics <i>and</i> probability on a local level to prevent any action would make it do something - attempting to affect it from outside of &quot;local space&quot; causes timing hiccups on your end that mean you end up missing.<br /> <br /> Using it as a shield doesn't work - the ways it tweaks reality mean that you can't use it as cover. Heck, try to use it as a hat rack some time - the outlandish ways you fail to put your hat on it will at least be good for a laugh. In general, it'll wind down in about hour - though it has a <i>nasty</i> tendency to wind itself if someone tries to damage it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T06:44:10-08:00","id":751311,"title":"","content":"<b>Summoning Circle</b> (Summon + Rip The Gates): This strange brass ring is lined in alternating Demonic and Angelic script (those who look really closely, and have been specially trained, might be able to tell the difference) and can be activated to call forth a being from one of the other realms. <b>Disclaimer</b>: while the Lambda will compel appearance, it does not compel cooperation or good behavior. Additional employment of the entity's Ban, Bane, and/or other warding is strongly recommended.<br /> <br /> <b>Combination Drive</b> (Merge + Demon Car): This Lambda is peculiar in that it only operates in a set with other like Lambdas. When these... devices... are installed in vehicles, their users can trigger them to combine their transformed automotives into a nightmarish juggernaut of steel, Demonic weaponry, and voided auto insurance. [<i>Go, go, Demonic Voltron!</i>]<br /> <br /> <b>Personal Heaven/Hell</b> (Solitary Confinement + Visions Of Heaven And Hell): This twisting, ephemeral seeming door leads one into their own personal Heaven, filled with all the delights their mind can imagine, or their own personal Hellscape, filled with all the torments that plague their subconscious. While each instance only leads one place, the doors are rarely labelled. Some Agencies use them to break recalcitrant subjects - by subjecting them to torment, withholding delights, or just afflicting them with uncertainty.<br /> <br /> <b>Super Happy Fun Bouncy Ball</b> (The Look + Apple of Discord): This nefarious rubber ball enthralls all who notice it, compelling them to stare enraptured into its depths until they fall unconscious. Just toss it into a crowded room and let the &quot;fun&quot; begin. Some variants have Affliction (keyed to Madness) used instead of The Look.<br /> <br /> <b>Golden Dulcinea Idol</b> (Apple of Discord + Addiction + No Quarter): This unnaturally plain looking gold (-plated) statue drives everyone who beholds it mad with desire for it, and will attempt to kill all competitors in an effort to be the sole possessor, then spending the rest of their efforts never leaving its presence. Makes for a great distraction or guard-catcher.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ant-Spy</b> (Animal Communication + Remote Link-Up): This tiny optical device lets the whoever places it upon an ant (Formicidae) remote control and see through the tiny creature's senses. Very useful for spying unawares. Alternate designs have been known to be constructed for flies (Musca domestica).<br /> <br /> <b>Angel Slayer</b> (Ephemeral Cover + Reality Enforcement): This blade seems to be both more and less <i>real</i> than everything around it. When striking an Angel, even one in Twilight, it disables their access to Numina for 5 turns (duration being replaced with each successful strike). Demons and Stigmatics are unable to use their own powers while holding the weapon, however.<br /> <br /> <b>Seeker Bomb</b> (Animal Messenger + Combustion): This torturous looking prod can transform hapless animals into target seeking incendiaries. After being branded, the user utters the target's name, and may speak a short message (message is optional - if not declared, the animal will repeat the first sentence it encounters; something that led a mage cabal on a wild goose chase for a month, trying to uncover the mystic significance of pigeons telling them to &quot;Eat At Joe's&quot; before undergoing spontaneously combustion). After delivering its message on contact with the target, the poor creature becomes highly flammable, often bursting into flames in the next moment and burning the target of the &quot;message&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Devouring Beacon</b> (Devour Infrastructure + Swarm + Hellhounds): This hive-like mass can be implanted inside a piece of active Infrastructure. Once set, it anchors itself and begins consuming the Infrastructure for Aether, while sending out a call to vermin in the area. Any that arrive near it get transformed into guardian cryptids and fed sustaining Aether. Eventually, the hive will fully consume the Infrastructure, and release a hoard of Aether-hungry cryptids into the surrounding area. In the meantime, it makes an excellent distraction/trap for any angel that comes to defend the parasitized Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-03-2015, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T10:15:14-08:00","id":751615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=746772#post746772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rip The Gates+Newton's Nightmares+Echoing Death=???</div> </div> </div> </div>So, did anyone actually have any ideas for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:24:04-08:00","id":751815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=751615#post751615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, did anyone actually have any ideas for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, looking at the components...<br /> Rip The Gates: Sends stuff to other realms.<br /> Newton's Nightmares: Plays around with inertia and gravity.<br /> Echoing Death: Kill someone and undo what they did.<br /> <br /> How about<b></b>: Creates a vortex that pulls all drawn within into the Underworld, and undoes their recent (or life's) actions. No one can tell you set off the device after it activated, nor knows anyone pulled inside was in the area.<br /> <br /> I'm sure this can be played around with more...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T00:44:36-08:00","id":762067,"title":"","content":"That did actually give me another idea:<br /> <br /> <b>Rip The Gates + Two Places At Once + Disintegrate</b><br /> <br /> Product: Literal Portal gun.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrible Avatar + Decoy + Context Matters</b><br /> <br /> Product: Your friends don't know how, but for as long as they've know you, you've had an imaginary demon friend. It's pretty spooky how you can talk to it through your pendant, but your imaginary friend seems like a pretty cool guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T10:29:28-08:00","id":763224,"title":"","content":"My Saboteur/Tempter hasn't made this one yet, but I have the embeds. The target item is mostly irrelevant with two exceptions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Small for purposes of package delivery</li> <li>Huge for purposes of grand display</li> </ol><b>Apple of Discord + No Quarter</b><br /> <br /> <i>Joey eyed the bike messenger as she held out the small box. Too small for a head, maybe a hand. He shook it and looked confused at the lightness of it. The messenger was sent packing when she tried to get Joey to sign for the package. He delivered it to the boss immediately.<br /> <br /> Giuseppe &quot;The Grater&quot; Gratelli looked up from his dinner.<br /> <br /> &quot;Joey, why you bother me with this? When you see a man eating, do you think 'Oh now's the time to give him something else to do?'&quot;<br /> <br /> The henchmen sheepishly reached for the box before he was slapped away. &quot;Chooch!&quot;<br /> <br /> Gi\u00f9 tore open the box to find a tissue paper-wrapped item no bigger than a cell phone, but seemed to be wavy instead of flat. The rest of his crime family looked on in silence from their place at the table. The tissue paper came off without issue to reveal a cheap 3x5 panel image of Giuseppe's wife, Caprice, laying nude in what was obviously a hotel bedroom. The odd shape of the medium somehow made the image more lurid.<br /> <br /> Caprice was out of her chair and screaming for the picture before anyone else could move. The capos soon jumped in, but not before Gi\u00f9 stabbed Marco with a dinner knife. Gunfire exploded from within Gratelli's as the bike messenger strolled down the block with a slight smile on her face.</i><br /> <br /> <b>OR</b><br /> <br /> <i>Cassandra could not believe her life! She finally got her sculptures the attention they deserved and now she was about to open her first major gallery. She owed everything to the old man in the slums who convinced her she could be a famous artist. The ratty brown bag &quot;contract&quot; he had her sign was just the metaphor she needed to see her true potential. Of course, she turned him away when he tried to ask her a favor later, but that was completely beside the point.<br /> <br /> The house lights dimmed and the spotlight beamed down as the cover was lifted. Cassandra couldn't believe her eyes. The smooth curves of her interpretation of the Mother Goddess were distorted into hard angles and jagged points...but she loved it. This bizarre creation was the most beautiful thing she had ever seen. One of the gallery guests approached the base and Cassandra jumped in front of her.<br /> <br /> &quot;Get back. This is mine and you can't take it from me!&quot; Cassandra stood defiant as several more guests seemed to move to touch the masterpiece. HER masterpiece.<br /> <br /> Cassandra fell unconscious after the champagne tray smashed into her face for the third time. The waitress turned away from the artist just in time to be slashed with a broken bottle. From an apartment window two blocks away, a young man took video of the chaos.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":2668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","user":"Asmenedas","date":".  Typo 11-11-2015, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T07:15:29-08:00","id":764911,"title":"","content":"That combo is always nice. You can add in so many other powers to tinker with its effects in different ways. <b>Addictive Presence</b> means even casual &quot;contact&quot; leaves a mark and brings victims back. <b>Inflict Stigmata</b> might soup up those caught in its web. <b>Hellhounds</b> definitely does, provided you can key it to ensnare animals. <b>Animate</b> let's it move on its own. <b>Force Relationship</b> (and <b>Open-and-Shut Case</b>) can do terrible things to those enthralled by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T13:06:32-08:00","id":765111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=762067#post762067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That did actually give me another idea:<br /> <br /> <b>Rip The Gates + Two Places At Once + Disintegrate</b><br /> <br /> Product: Literal Portal gun.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrible Avatar + Decoy + Context Matters</b><br /> <br /> Product: Your friends don't know how, but for as long as they've know you, you've had an imaginary demon friend. It's pretty spooky how you can talk to it through your pendant, but your imaginary friend seems like a pretty cool guy.</div> </div> </div> </div> Shouldn't the Portal Gun have Newton's Nightmares instead of Disintegrate? The latter Exploit would make permanent holes in walls that lead to the next room over, not the moon. In the games, whenever you close a portal, the surface it was placed on remains intact.<br /> <br /> The former Exploit would explain why your inertia is unaffected while going through portals (&quot;speedy thing goes in, speedy thing comes out&quot;, as GLaDOS said), and why the Portal Gun can levitate objects.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, shouldn't it be Behind The Curtain instead of Rip The Gates? The former Exploit is for teleporting between two points in regular space (where Infrastructure is present), while the latter opens portals to alternate planes of reality. Granted, you could create some interesting scenarios by saying that the Portal Gun uses the Invisible Realms as shortcuts. What would happen if someone mishandled, or God forbid, broke it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-15-2015, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T08:25:25-08:00","id":767089,"title":"","content":"<b>Inflict Stigmata + Right Tools, Right Job</b><br /> <br /> When one straps this watch-like device onto one's wrist and activates it, small prongs and wires begin to burrow into the user's flesh. It's uncomfortable, but not necessarily painful. The Gadget grants the user a Supernatural Merit most relevant to whatever the user's situation may be, remaining for as long as the device is connected to the wearer's flesh. A slightly different version of this Lambda exists, replacing Inflict Stigmata with Show of Power, but for most, the persistent nightmares aren't worth its boon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T17:39:47-08:00","id":768197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=765111#post765111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Shouldn't the Portal Gun have Newton's Nightmares instead of Disintegrate? The latter Exploit would make permanent holes in walls that lead to the next room over, not the moon. In the games, whenever you close a portal, the surface it was placed on remains intact.<br /> <br /> The former Exploit would explain why your inertia is unaffected while going through portals (&quot;speedy thing goes in, speedy thing comes out&quot;, as GLaDOS said), and why the Portal Gun can levitate objects.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, shouldn't it be Behind The Curtain instead of Rip The Gates? The former Exploit is for teleporting between two points in regular space (where Infrastructure is present), while the latter opens portals to alternate planes of reality. Granted, you could create some interesting scenarios by saying that the Portal Gun uses the Invisible Realms as shortcuts. What would happen if someone mishandled, or God forbid, broke it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use whatever you prefer. The whole Lamdba system is quite freeform realistically. There's a lot of conceptual overlap in the different embeds and exploits so there's no one purely &quot;correct&quot; way to do most of these examples, especially if you want different side case effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T11:32:44-08:00","id":772421,"title":"","content":"<b>Remote Control</b> (The Word + Show of Power): This alien looking device operates by pointing it at a supernatural target and dictating the power you want them to perform. If the signal successfully overpowers their control <i>and</i> they actually have the ability to perform the task commanded, they do so upon their next action, using their own talent (ie. their own dice pools and rules, not Show of Power's capped totals).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T10:41:34-08:00","id":822498,"title":"","content":"Tools Into Toys + Right Tools Right Job + Raw Materials + Efficiency = <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-914\" target=\"_blank\"><b>SCP-914</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:34:07-08:00","id":822550,"title":"","content":"If SCP-914 is a (what would that be, Third Order?) Lambda, then SCP-882 is Logistical Infrastructure run rampant, more or less strip-mining Essence. It's probably watched over by an Imperative, or by a Rank 1 Angel. The Church of the Broken God is a goldmine for God-Machine related material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T12:27:19-08:00","id":822607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=822550#post822550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If SCP-914 is a (what would that be, Third Order?) Lambda, then SCP-882 is Logistical Infrastructure run rampant, more or less strip-mining Essence. It's probably watched over by an Imperative, or by a Rank 1 Angel. The Church of the Broken God is a goldmine for God-Machine related material.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very true. The God-Machine could be responsible for so many SCPs, it's crazy. One example off the top of my head is a Cryptid similar to <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-745\" target=\"_blank\"><b>SCP-745</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T12:54:25-08:00","id":822645,"title":"","content":"Oh, now that's really cool. In my Demon games I usually depict the Church of the Broken God as a multinational God-Machine cult on the verge of going public and becoming recognized as a religion. I think I set them up as a Mystery Cult a while back, but I'll have to go digging through my notes to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T10:22:47-08:00","id":823476,"title":"","content":"Can you combine Demonic Form Gadgets with Embedded and Exploited Gadgets? I was thinking that, if the Rivet Arm Modification cannot be affected with a direct activation of the Hellfire Exploit, I could instead make a Hellfire Gadget and attach it to my Rivet Arm through the Subsumed Gadget Merit. The same could theoretically done to Claws And Fangs or Blade Hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T10:57:18-08:00","id":823508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=823476#post823476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you combine Demonic Form Gadgets with Embedded and Exploited Gadgets? I was thinking that, if the Rivet Arm Modification cannot be affected with a direct activation of the Hellfire Exploit, I could instead make a Hellfire Gadget and attach it to my Rivet Arm through the Subsumed Gadget Merit. The same could theoretically done to Claws And Fangs or Blade Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing why not, other than Form Gadgets being rarer and thus, more precious. You can't just make another as easily if you foul up the Installation.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of how to do One-Shot Form Gadgets and Lambdas. I really wish the name/term Knockoff wasn't already taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:27:52-08:00","id":831810,"title":"","content":"Here's an over the top idea:<br /> <br /> First, acquire the Rivet Arm Modifivation. Then, create a Lambda Gadget consisting of Solitary Confinement + Hellhound + Hellfire + Swarm. Said Gadget will contain a Cryptid meant to self-destruct in an explosion of multiplying, all-devouring nanomachines. Insert the Gadget into your Rivet Arm with the Subsumed Gadget Merit. You have a miniature nuke ready to fire. Just be careful where you point it, and be very clear with the conditions that deactivate the nanomachines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:35:38-08:00","id":831864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=831810#post831810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an over the top idea:<br /> <br /> First, acquire the Rivet Arm Modifivation. Then, create a Lambda Gadget consisting of Solitary Confinement + Hellhound + Hellfire + Swarm. Said Gadget will contain a Cryptid meant to self-destruct in an explosion of multiplying, all-devouring nanomachines. Insert the Gadget into your Rivet Arm with the Subsumed Gadget Merit. You have a miniature nuke ready to fire. Just be careful where you point it, and be very clear with the conditions that deactivate the nanomachines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potential problem: that's a 3rd Order Lambda, which are only hypothesized to exist. Also, I don't think Subsume gadget works that way. At the point of making a 3O Lambda, why don't you just make the thing self-guided?<br /> <br /> Drop the Solitary Confinement, and just make sure to summon animals/swarms via a different mechanism. Or use Deep Pockets. <hr /><br /> Hmmm. <u>Rain of Blood</u> + <u>Hellfire</u> = <i><b>Rain of Fire</b></i>, for when you absolutely must draw attention to yourself with old-school destruction.<br /> <br /> Heck, Rain of Blood + <i>Anything</i> can get pretty sick. Affliction, Hellhounds, Riot, Inflict Stigmata, Ultimatum, Time Stop... <hr /><br /> What about using <u>Affliction</u> + <u>Riot</u> to make a Hate-Plague?<br /> <hr /><br /> General question: Does anyone think Reality Enforcement can be combined with anything, or that it would shut down itself? Because <u>Reality Enforcement</u> + <u>Solitary Confinement</u> would make a great Angel/Demon prison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-17-2016, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:01:21-08:00","id":831941,"title":"","content":"<b>Oooooo</b>. <u>4 Minutes Ago</u> + <u>Ripple</u> + <u>Rain of Blood</u> = the <b>Ground Hog Day Device</b>. After triggering, it resets time in the area to the previous day, repeating each day (not merely 4 minutes, or at reduced effect, because 2nd Order Lambda - F you standard rules). Largely inspired by circumstances in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825315-the-town-that-ran-like-clockwork-demon-actual-play\">The Town That Ran Like Clockwork</a>.<br /> <hr /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Build <u>Rain of Blood</u> + <u>Like the Movies</u> Lambda.</li> <li>Avoid getting killed by Angels and activate it.</li> <li>...?</li> <li>Profit!</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-17-2016, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:27:05-08:00","id":831970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=831864#post831864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Potential problem: that's a 3rd Order Lambda, which are only hypothesized to exist. Also, I don't think Subsume gadget works that way. At the point of making a 3O Lambda, why don't you just make the thing self-guided?<br /> <br /> Drop the Solitary Confinement, and just make sure to summon animals/swarms via a different mechanism. Or use Deep Pockets. <hr /><br /> Hmmm. <u>Rain of Blood</u> + <u>Hellfire</u> = <i><b>Rain of Fire</b></i>, for when you absolutely must draw attention to yourself with old-school destruction.<br /> <br /> Heck, Rain of Blood + <i>Anything</i> can get pretty sick. Affliction, Hellhounds, Riot, Inflict Stigmata, Ultimatum, Time Stop... <hr /><br /> What about using <u>Affliction</u> + <u>Riot</u> to make a Hate-Plague?<br /> <hr /><br /> General question: Does anyone think Reality Enforcement can be combined with anything, or that it would shut down itself? Because <u>Reality Enforcement</u> + <u>Solitary Confinement</u> would make a great Angel/Demon prison.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're right, Subsumed Gadget does something else. If I want to combine Lambdas with my Demonic Form abilities, I'd need to come up with a new Merit.<br /> <br /> Rain Of Blood + The Word + Ultimatum would be terrifying. If one person in the targeted group disobeys the command, everyone would turn into a statue.<br /> <br /> That Angel/Demon prison might work, and it could also become a virtual reality chamber with the addition of Visions Of Heaven And Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:43:09-08:00","id":831985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=831970#post831970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're right, Subsumed Gadget does something else. If I want to combine Lambdas with my Demonic Form abilities, I'd need to come up with a new Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only there was some place to put it... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=831970#post831970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rain Of Blood + The Word + Ultimatum would be terrifying. If one person in the targeted group disobeys the command, everyone would turn into a statue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even sure The Word would be necessary, since it would affect everyone caught in the Rain, anyways (and if the Ultimatum is &quot;attack this C&amp;C Infrastructure or turn into Salt/Stone/Uranium&quot;, then the Demon doesn't <i>want</i> one &quot;no&quot; to spoil their plan). The Word might allow some interesting alternative consequences to failing the Ultimatum, though...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=831970#post831970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Angel/Demon prison might work, and it could also become a virtual reality chamber with the addition of Visions Of Heaven And Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've got a less anti-Angel/Demon version earlier in the thread. Not sure if Visions of Heaven And Hell work on Angels/Demons, though. If you want the target screwed <i>and dead</i>, the Analyst &quot;Going Loud&quot; Exploit Combo examples had Solitary Confinement + Hellfire (or was it Incendiary?) to ignite the oubliette in flames, so you could add that in for fun*.<br /> <br /> * = For Dwarf Fortress values of Fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:57:13-08:00","id":831997,"title":"","content":"<u>Rain of Blood</u> (I love this Exploit even more now) + <u>Halo</u> = Healing Rain. Because Demons don't <i>have</i> to be pricks. Unless they are solely using it for the sleep effect.<br /> <br /> <u>Rain of Blood</u> + <u>Context Matters</u> = Pay No Attention To The Weird Crap Going On device.<br /> <br /> <u>Rain of Blood</u> + <u>Disintegrate</u> = Back To Nature (A.K.A Nudifier) Field.<br /> <br /> <u>Rain of Blood</u> + <u>Ephemeral Cover</u> = Exorcise Town.<br /> <br /> <u>Rain of Blood</u> + <u>Raze Infrastructure</u> = Pissing Off The Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-17-2016, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T13:07:45-08:00","id":832005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=831997#post831997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Rain of Blood</u> + <u>Ephemeral Cover</u> = Exorcise Town.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you meant &quot;Implant Haunted Climate&quot;. I agree with and loved the rest, though!<br /> <br /> How about this: Rain Of Blood + Apple Of Discord = money from the skies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T13:28:18-08:00","id":832016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=832005#post832005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think you meant &quot;Implant Haunted Climate&quot;. I agree with and loved the rest, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, part 1 of Ephemeral Cover rips the Corpus from Ephemerals. Part 2 lets you turn it into a Cover. Given the context, I'm thinking the Rain melts Corpus like the Wicked Witch of the West. Great for clearing out pesky ghosts and spirits. And for pissing off every Pack in the area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=832005#post832005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about this: Rain Of Blood + Apple Of Discord = money from the skies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apple of Discord doesn't <i>make</i> money, just makes people want the target after seeing it. Rain of Blood could allow it to affect more the just viewers, though (you shall all seek the Maltese Falcon). Or combo it with Raw Materials and make money (that people greedily obsess over) fall from the skies.<br /> <br /> Though I wonder if you can use some weird combination to make money from the general property damage of the storm. Call it &quot;Wealth Redistribution&quot;. Maybe with Break to Heal or Raw Materials as a Near Field Effect?<br /> <br /> ...And now I'm thinking of cash spilling from destroyed objects like blocks in a Lego game...<br /> <br /> Annnnd, now I'm trying to think what combos would be necessary to create a weapon Lambda that turns defeated enemies into cash, like they are pinatas...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-17-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T14:49:29-08:00","id":834641,"title":"","content":"Game Nerd Question: if I wanted to replicate the &quot;Apple of Eden&quot; from Assassin's creed as a Lambda Gadget, what would you guys suggest it have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:38:48-08:00","id":835039,"title":"","content":"Had to look it up. Seems like the primary component is mental control (illusions can simply be wrapped into that). I'm thinking The Word might be a key component. Or Sermon. Nothing I read lead me to think it has any great range, or vastly different powers. It might not even need to be a Lambda (an Exploited Gadget with Sermon might replicate it to a fair degree).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T09:22:59-08:00","id":835102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=835039#post835039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had to look it up. Seems like the primary component is mental control (illusions can simply be wrapped into that). I'm thinking The Word might be a key component. Or Sermon. Nothing I read lead me to think it has any great range, or vastly different powers. It might not even need to be a Lambda (an Exploited Gadget with Sermon might replicate it to a fair degree).</div> </div> </div> </div>The official wiki says: Illusion projection, Mind-control, Physical manipulation, Negate effects of staves of Eden, Knowledge, Possibility to see or create Calculations (Future Eventualities)<br /> <br /> What about a combo of <b>Apple of Discord + Download Knowledge + Sermon, </b>and/or + The Word?<br /> <br /> Edit: In hindsight, this might end up being a Second-Order Lambda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 02-22-2016, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:39:03-07:00","id":848227,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Rod of Necromancy</b></u> (<u>Animate</u> + <u>Hellhounds</u>): This warped, visibly haunted rod has still successfully been passed off as an elaborate prop at a convention a time or two. At least, until it touches a dead body and reanimates the corpse into an unholy Cryptid-zombie. No amount of &quot;special effects&quot; talk can explain away a shambling Necro-morph looking thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-16-2016, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:48:32-07:00","id":848392,"title":"","content":"Sword of Michael (Inferno + Terrible Avatar + Download Knowledge): This deeply ornate medieval hilt appears to be a piece of some museum collection until one looks closer and sees the modern components and ignition switch. When activated a blade of Hellfire erupts from the hilt, but more importantly the light that this blade projects coalesces into a furious burning angel that will battle at the side of the wielder. The activator also instantly becomes aware of how to weild the blade in battle. Whst this gadget lacks in subtlety it more than makes up in its ability to destroy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T14:51:08-07:00","id":848425,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Pandora's Box</b></u> (<u>Cause and Effect</u> + <u>Strength Through Adversity</u>): Few enjoy opening this dreadful container. Those who do find a series of coincidences causing their entire world to crumble around them. Though those who survive the process often end up fabulously rewarded for their troubles.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Genie In A Bottle</b></u> (<u>Terrible Avatar</u> + <u>Show Of Power</u>): This cloudy glass bottle swirls with smoke and ash. When opened, a terrible being emerges that will fulfill 3 of the user's requests before becoming inert (until take up by a new user).<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Mark Of Cain</b></u> (<u>Soul Brand</u> + <u>Eye For An Eye</u> + <u>Ripple</u>): Whenever the bearer of this terrible brand is dealt harm, that harm is also visited upon the doer, at greater intensity.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Necronomicon, Abridged</b></u> (<u>Rain Of Blood</u> + <u>Animate</u> + <u>Hellhounds</u>): If someone can manage to invoke the words listed in this dark tome (made a bit complicated by said words crawling across the page at random), they invoke a terrible storm that animates all corpses in the area into terrifying monstrosities. <br /> <br /> <u><b>The Soul Taker</b></u> (<u>Echoing Death</u> + <u>Break To Heal</u>): Striking someone with this twisted, black metal blade unmakes their victim and restores their own health from the energies of their annihilated foe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-17-2016, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T18:13:40-07:00","id":908019,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Duplicatron</b></u> (<u>Decoy</u> + <u>Terrible Avatar</u>): It looks like a phone booth from hell, and inside are far more needles and instruments than you'd care to count. Baalzebul said that when you stepped in, it'd analyze you, and then something cool would happen. If you didn't owe him, you wouldn't be testing it. So you step in, get jabbed, poked and prodded a bunch, shoved unceremoniously out, and then after five terrifying minutes of the entire workshop shaking and filling with smoke, you step out of the machine again. It's not just a cheap ripoff, either. It's a full-on copy. The poor sap died a week later, and the machine had been totally blown out, but damn is Baalzebul isn't a clever bastard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 07-09-2016, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T19:29:23-07:00","id":908053,"title":"","content":"Has anyone already tried translating infernal objects from Exalted into Lambdas or gadgets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T07:56:42-07:00","id":909167,"title":"","content":"Maybe someone can help me with something. I'm looking to use a Second-Order Lambda as a centerpiece for my Las Vegas chronicle. In brief, I wanted to create a setting in which the Demons &quot;win&quot; and craft a kind of Hell. As such, they used The Wheel to banish the machine and cause its angels to Fall within Vegas. It essentially looks like a roulette wheel but with a certain design asthetic that also resembles a satellite dish. Basically, the function of the Wheel (also called the Beast, since if you add up all the numbers in roulette you get a total of 666) is to draw upon all the sins and vices within the city and &quot;broadcast&quot; them over the same occult frequencies the God-Machine uses to direct Its angels. In other words, the Wheel scrambles the omniscient will of God with the petty hopes and sins of humanity. An Angel has difficulty discerning the desires of It from the desperate and petty vices of humanity. In effect, if an angel isn't already disconnected from the Machine as an Exile, it can only exist within the city limits of Vegas a certain amount of time (usually a few minutes, at best a few hours) before the Wheel's signal drives it into a Fall. <br /> <br /> Now, as to what the Unchained do with their new freedom the Wheel gives them...heh. Well, consider what happens in normal history sometimes after a revolution succeeds in opposing a government. The Reign of Terror, the Communist Revolution (and Stalin's regime)....let's just say Hell isn't always what its cracked up to be. &quot;Be careful what you wish for&quot; is one of my themes. But more on that some other time.<br /> <br /> That's the intended FUNCTION. But I started designing this Lambda backwards, getting inspired by the concept and working out the details later. Any advice on what combination of Embeds could result in this powerful effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T08:03:13-07:00","id":909169,"title":"","content":"Imagine seems like it could be a component, due to how it shows a world without the G-M. Interference scrambles its sensors, so that might also play a part.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Though it's interesting to see you work on this again. Also, I'd think of working it as either a rare Demon-made Infrastructure or the core of a network of &quot;reprogramed&quot; Infrastructures, but this seems like it also works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 06-07-2016, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T09:28:18-07:00","id":909219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=909167#post909167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe someone can help me with something. I'm looking to use a Second-Order Lambda as a centerpiece for my Las Vegas chronicle. In brief, I wanted to create a setting in which the Demons &quot;win&quot; and craft a kind of Hell. As such, they used The Wheel to banish the machine and cause its angels to Fall within Vegas. It essentially looks like a roulette wheel but with a certain design asthetic that also resembles a satellite dish. Basically, the function of the Wheel (also called the Beast, since if you add up all the numbers in roulette you get a total of 666) is to draw upon all the sins and vices within the city and &quot;broadcast&quot; them over the same occult frequencies the God-Machine uses to direct Its angels. In other words, the Wheel scrambles the omniscient will of God with the petty hopes and sins of humanity. An Angel has difficulty discerning the desires of It from the desperate and petty vices of humanity. In effect, if an angel isn't already disconnected from the Machine as an Exile, it can only exist within the city limits of Vegas a certain amount of time (usually a few minutes, at best a few hours) before the Wheel's signal drives it into a Fall.<br /> <br /> Now, as to what the Unchained do with their new freedom the Wheel gives them...heh. Well, consider what happens in normal history sometimes after a revolution succeeds in opposing a government. The Reign of Terror, the Communist Revolution (and Stalin's regime)....let's just say Hell isn't always what its cracked up to be. &quot;Be careful what you wish for&quot; is one of my themes. But more on that some other time.<br /> <br /> That's the intended FUNCTION. But I started designing this Lambda backwards, getting inspired by the concept and working out the details later. Any advice on what combination of Embeds could result in this powerful effect?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Potential Components</b>:<br /> <u>Imagine</u> (shows world without God-Machine)<br /> <u>Interference</u> (scrambles G-M signals)<br /> <u>Cause and Effect</u> (Vice causes Angelic Fall)<br /> <u>Visions of Heaven and Hell</u> (leverages mental influence)<br /> <u>The Word</u> (&quot;Fall&quot;, maybe?)<br /> <u>Solitary Confinement</u> (but keyed to only isolate the &quot;G-M Signal&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=909169#post909169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Though it's interesting to see you work on this again. Also, I'd think of working it as either a rare Demon-made Infrastructure or the core of a network of &quot;reprogramed&quot; Infrastructures, but this seems like it also works.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lambda could be &quot;installed&quot; into Infrastructure, enabling the signal to be city-wide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:18:31-07:00","id":928287,"title":"","content":"Question: if one were to make a gadget that replicated Merge, and it was used by a stigmatic, what possible effects could you try for, Near-field effects included?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:51:25-07:00","id":928311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=928287#post928287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: if one were to make a gadget that replicated Merge, and it was used by a stigmatic, what possible effects could you try for, Near-field effects included?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shared Supernatural Merits, maybe? If it is part of a Lambda, it would depend on what the other part is. I've got notes for one that is <u>Merge</u> + <u>Show Of Power</u> (Or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=837729#post837729\">Fuel Leak</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=849249#post849249\">Finders, Keepers</a>, or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=837729#post837729\">Aether Burn</a>) that lets supernatural fuel stats be shared and converted between a group. This specific one would be for the Demon to assume Demonic Form and use the Aether collection to help recharge her &quot;sister&quot;'s Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:06:52-07:00","id":928411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196703-lambda-gadgets?p=928311#post928311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shared Supernatural Merits, maybe? If it is part of a Lambda, it would depend on what the other part is. I've got notes for one that is <u>Merge</u> + <u>Show Of Power</u> (Or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=837729#post837729\">Fuel Leak</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=849249#post849249\">Finders, Keepers</a>, or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/837712-homebrew-embeds-and-exploits?p=837729#post837729\">Aether Burn</a>) that lets supernatural fuel stats be shared and converted between a group. This specific one would be for the Demon to assume Demonic Form and use the Aether collection to help recharge her &quot;sister&quot;'s Mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, but I was thinking more about the opportunities for body horror. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:26:19-07:00","id":928424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\